- op: discuss  # d5e6
  at: '2026-09-17T23:05:43Z'  # d5e6
  by: agent  # d5e6
  actor: jgstern_agent  # d5e6
  clock: 4  # d5e6
  nonce: d5e6  # d5e6
  message: "SATISFIED. Positive evidence, not non-reproduction.\n\nTHE FILED FIRST STEP WAS REACHABILITY, and it is now measured. Invoked\nrust-analyzer on ~/whole_bunch_of_repos/aardvark-dns and counted descriptor\nkinds directly out of the SCIP index (681 SymbolInformation entries):\n\n    <local>          500\n    method            80\n    term              48\n    type              25\n    namespace         18\n    type_parameter    10     <-- REACHABLE\n    parameter          0\n    meta               0\n\nSo type_parameter is NOT dead vocabulary. It is filtered before minting on\nTHIS crate only because those entries carry no Definition-role occurrence --\nscip_index_to_symbols minted 669 symbols, all registered kinds. A survey alone\nwould have shown a clean artifact and hidden the fact; the row's instinct to\ndemand reachability before a verdict was right.\n\nunknown IS unreachable, and provably rather than by sampling: DescriptorKind\nis a closed Enum with 8 members, _KIND_MAP covered all 8, and every producer\nin descriptor.py constructs from the enum. Verified in code:\n  DescriptorKind members: 8, covered by _KIND_MAP: 8, unmapped: NONE\n\nTHE FIX, per value:\n\n  parameter       REGISTERED. Names a source-language syntactic construct\n  type_parameter  directly, which is what ADR-0027's axiom asks of a value.\n                  Registered rather than folded.\n\n  meta            MAPPED to \"declaration\", the registry's own declared\n                  catch-all (\"Generic declaration (catch-all for\n                  non-categorized syntactic forms)\"). SCIP's META is an\n                  encoding category, not a language construct, so it could\n                  never be a registered kind under the axiom. NOT folded into\n                  \"attribute\", which the registry defines as a data member (a\n                  Python class attribute) -- that would have been a guess\n                  dressed as a verdict. RE-EVALUATION TRIGGER written at the\n                  mapping: zero META descriptors observed; the first real\n                  instance should be inspected for a specific kind.\n\n  unknown         REMOVED. The .get(..., \"unknown\") fallback is now a direct\n                  subscript. A KeyError on a future ninth DescriptorKind is\n                  louder and more truthful than silently minting a kind\n                  nothing describes.\n\nTHE GATES THE DICT NEVER HAD (packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/\ntest_scip_kind_map_conformance.py): every _KIND_MAP value is a registered\nSymbol.kind, and the map is total over DescriptorKind. Both have a positive\ncontrol that mutates the map and asserts each gate rejects it. This is the\nstructural answer to the root_cause on this row -- axis_drift could not see a\nDICT, so the gate lives next to the dict instead.\n\nVERIFICATION: 14758 passed; mypy ratchet 667 (delta +0). docs/schema.json and\ndocs/concept-axes.md regenerated (both embed the kind registry).\n\nNOT CLAIMED: that parameter/meta are unreachable. They were unobserved on ONE\ncrate, which is why neither was deprecated -- both now resolve to registered\nvalues whatever they turn out to carry."  # d5e6
